    <detaileddescription>
<para>Plays streaming TTS audio from a server-side agent through a USoundWaveProcedural fed by a hidden UAudioComponent.</para>
<para>Add it to the same actor as a <ref refid="class_u_tryll_agent_component" kindref="compound">UTryllAgentComponent</ref>, or assign it to the agent&apos;s Speaker slot; the agent forwards TTS audio frames here. If the workflow speaks and the actor has no speaker, the agent creates one.</para>
<sect1 id="class_u_tryll_speaker_component_1autotoc_md0_1s1"><sect2 id="class_u_tryll_speaker_component_1autotoc_md0">
<title>Threading</title><para>HandleFormat and HandleAudio fire on the game thread (drained by UTryllSubsystem::Tick). USoundWaveProcedural::QueueAudio is internally thread-safe — it copies into its own consumer queue, which the audio mixer thread drains.</para>
</sect2></sect1>
<sect1 id="class_u_tryll_speaker_component_1autotoc_md1_1s1"><sect2 id="class_u_tryll_speaker_component_1autotoc_md1">
<title>End-of-stream</title><para>TtsAudioFrame carries no is_final flag — the turn ends with TurnComplete, which the agent forwards to HandleTurnComplete. The procedural sound never finishes on its own (it plays silence when its queue is empty), so after HandleTurnComplete the component ticks until the queue has drained, then fires OnTtsAudioFinished. </para>
</sect2></sect1>
    </detaileddescription>
